module

public import Theory.SpecificGroups.Janko4.Model.Cardinality.LocalInvolutionCensus.Fusion.Tables

/-!
# Matrix witnesses for the max2 square-one exclusion

The four forward lift matrices reuse the existing census witnesses. The
thirteen proposed inverse factor matrices use balanced lookup for packed-row
calculation. This module makes no assertion that these matrices evaluate the
inverse source words; that assertion is a separate matrix certificate.

The factors come from the unchanged ATLAS `J4G1-max2W1` program, attributed
to R. A. Wilson, S. J. Nickerson and J. N. Bray. See the preserved source and
attribution under `TwoCoreCentralizer/source/README.md` and the reproducible
generator in `Coverage/source/`. The census motivation is Aschbacher--Smith,
`refs/quasithin.pdf`, printed pp.64--65, A.6.1--4.
-/

@[expose] public section
namespace Janko4.Cardinality.LocalInvolutionCensus.FiberCensus.Forest.Coverage
open Janko4.GeneratorCertificates
open OuterReduction.FixedGenerator.NormalizerSquares.TwoCoreCentralizerData

